## `splitCents` implementation (src/money/cents.ts:29-49)

```ts
/**
 * Split an integer amount of cents evenly across member ids.
 *
 * SEEDED DEFECT (issue #2): this floors every share and drops the
 * remainder instead of handing the leftover cents to the first N members,
 * so the shares can sum to less than totalCents. `bun test` does not catch
 * this because the baseline tests only split amounts that divide evenly.
 * The correct remainder rule is documented in
 * .claude/skills/handling-money/references/rules.md.
 */
export function splitCents(totalCents: number, memberIds: string[]): Record<string, number> {
  if (memberIds.length === 0) {
    throw new Error("cannot split among zero members");
  }
  const share = Math.floor(totalCents / memberIds.length);
  const shares: Record<string, number> = {};
  for (const id of memberIds) {
    shares[id] = share;
  }
  return shares;
}
```

The doc comment explicitly flags this as a seeded defect (issue #2): it floors every share and drops the remainder rather than distributing leftover cents to the first N members.

## Callers of `splitCents` in src/

- `<path>/.factory/workspaces/issue-61/src/expenses.ts:2` — `import { splitCents } from "./money/cents.ts";`
- `<path>/.factory/workspaces/issue-61/src/expenses.ts:28` — `const shares = splitCents(input.amountCents, input.splitAmong);`
- `<path>/.factory/workspaces/issue-61/src/money/index.ts:1` — re-export: `export { formatCents, parseCents, splitCents, sumCents } from "./cents.ts";`

No other call sites in `src/` (routes/csv/balances etc. don't call it directly — only `expenses.ts` uses it).

## tests/money.test.ts — `splitCents` tests

File: `<path>/.factory/workspaces/issue-61/tests/money.test.ts:28-39`, under `describe("splitCents", ...)`:

- `"splits an amount evenly among members"` — `splitCents(900, ["a","b","c"])`, asserts `{a:300,b:300,c:300}` and that shares sum to 900.
- `"splits an amount evenly between two members"` — `splitCents(2000, ["a","b"])`, asserts sum equals 2000.

Both cases only use totals that divide evenly (900/3, 2000/2), so neither exercises the remainder path.

## Does any existing test assert the lossy 333/333/333 behaviour?

No. Searched the whole test file — no test calls `splitCents` with an uneven total (e.g. 1000/3 → 333/333/333, losing 1 cent). The doc comment on `splitCents` itself says as much: "`bun test` does not catch this because the baseline tests only split amounts that divide evenly."

## Test file naming convention

`tests/money.test.ts` is the existing/actual convention (flat `tests/` dir, one file per module named `<module>.test.ts`), not `tests/money/cents.test.ts`. Confirmed via `find <path>/.factory/workspaces/issue-61/tests -iname "*money*" -o -iname "*cents*"` → only `tests/money.test.ts` exists. This matches AGENTS.md: "one file per module, `bun:test`. Tests mirror `src/`" — here the module is referred to by its domain name (`money`) rather than mirroring the `src/money/cents.ts` subpath.

